      "role": "user",
      "content": "Actually, that still feels a little bit generic. Is there any way to make it sound a bit more \"human\" or less like a standard HR script? Maybe something that acknowledges the specific \"vibe\" or culture of the team we have? I don't want it to be awkward, just less formal.",
